The formula StartsAtZero is a state-level formula, but it was used as a PROPERTY (or PROPERTIES), where a temporal formula is typically expected. State-level formulas used as PROPERTY or PROPERTIES are only checked in the initial state. To verify that the formula StartsAtZero holds in all states of every behavior, use INVARIANT StartsAtZero instead. Alternatively, applying the "always" temporal operator ([]) to the state-level formula StartsAtZero changes it into a temporal formula, asserting that StartsAtZero holds in all states of every behavior. See https://explain.tlapl.us/invariants-and-properties for additional details.
